#---
# purpose: A lambda that closes over a tuple of one shape or another, handed to Enum.map, runs the arm for the shape it holds on the interpreter, the JIT and a built program
# root: main/0
# assert.metric.semantic.activations: 5
# assert.metric.semantic.executables: 5
# assert.metric.semantic.callsites: 7
# assert.metric.call_edges.count: 7
# oracle: self
# oracle.stamp: b804559d557ee28b
#---
#
# `default` is `{:a, 1}` from one caller and `{:k}` from the other. The lambda
# is built once per call and holds whichever tuple that call produced, but the
# walk plans one body for each shape. Enum.map reaches the body through a
# dispatch whose arms are the two shapes. The closure's code word is the same
# for both arms, so the arm is chosen by reading the captured tuple.
defmodule Main do
  def tagged(flag) do
    default = if flag, do: {:a, 1}, else: {:k}
    Enum.map([1], fn r -> {default, r} end)
  end

  def main() do
    IO.inspect(tagged(true))
    IO.inspect(tagged(false))
  end
end

Main.main()
